rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All runtime-native workflows must conform to the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model, maintaining a strict separation of concerns between orchestration, reasoning,
    and knowledge access.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maturity levels and decision statuses must be interpreted consistently;
    exploring/proposed items map to NEXT, while stable/accepted items map to DONE.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created with a 'supporting' scope by default and validated
    through evidence before being considered for 'core' status.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: To maintain architectural clarity, patterns must not be merged or consolidated
    if they belong to different architectural layers (e.g., execution vs. governance).
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core requires strong, observable evidence from multiple
    sources or systems to ensure architectural stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work items are the authoritative source for planning state;
    all generated artifacts must derive their status from these records.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All decisions must use the structured YAML ADR schema rather than unstructured
    narrative text to enable machine processing and consistency.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must utilize the shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating workspace-level governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes foundational semantic rules for architecture artifacts, distinguishing
    between intent, decision, and system state.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence to ensure traceability and grounding.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the resolution model where Global Rules override Project Rules,
    and Project Rules override Prompt Rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures human-in-the-loop control; architectural decisions are proposed
    by the system but must be explicitly decided by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Governance artifacts like AEM and AID serve as summaries; they must not
    be used as the authoritative source of truth.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Decision Records (ADR) are the primary source of truth for
    decisions; all other representations must be derived from them.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Signals must satisfy recurrence, impact, reusability, and stability criteria
    before promotion to a pattern.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Decisions must be stored as structured ADR files before they are reflected
    in any other architecture maps or documents.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of architecture items must be programmatically derived
    from their underlying decision status.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must always align with and never contradict
    existing ADR decisions.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are restricted to foundational primitives; specific implementation
    strategies cannot be promoted to core status.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
